WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
I think there's little question that heatwaves&nbsp;
are becoming more frequent and they're getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.240
longer and they're getting hotter and one of&nbsp;
the questions we always get is what can you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.440
do about it? I think there's obvious answers&nbsp;
you want to stay inside and out of the heat as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.520
much as possible, but you're really also got&nbsp;
to think about your hydration. Even if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.380
are a young healthy person think about hydrating&nbsp;
throughout the day and if you're outside really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.880
making sure you're amping up your hydration to&nbsp;
at least a cup every 20 minutes. Think about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.460
lighter meals through the day that can help&nbsp;
you stay cooler especially at night as can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.980
avoiding alcohol in the evening. Also, when you&nbsp;
think about heat also think about the humidity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.380
You want to cool your environment but also you&nbsp;
want to take out as much humidity as possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.720
that lets the sweat off your skin actually&nbsp;
evaporate and cool you. And finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:55.200
still exercise, still be active but probably&nbsp;
frame shift those things to earlier in the day.

